01:05:57.000 --> 01:07:27.000
Two eminent pathologists studied the bone fragments that were discovered in the remains of the fire at the 183-mile gate. They confirmed that the non-artificial teeth were human, with one proving to be a molar tooth. Some of the smaller bones were suspected to be human finger or toe bones, although the pathologists couldn't conclusively rule out the possibility that they were from animal pores. The few skull fragments were fitted together, and it was determined they had most likely come from a Caucasian male. These skull fragments, along with the teeth, were the only decisive evidence that the fires had indeed contained human remains. On January 7, 1932, Snowy Rolls, aka John Thomas Smith, was formally charged with the murder of Louis Caron, and a mandatory coroner's inquest was ordered. On January 9, the media reported that earlier the previous year, Snowy had made two suicide attempts while in the Makathara lockup. Constable Penn told the Western Argus newspaper that he'd found Snowy attempting to hang himself in his cell, at which point Snowy also admitted that he'd tried taking strychnine, a highly toxic poison typically used as a pesticide.
两位杰出的病理学家研究了在183英里门火灾残骸中发现的骨头碎片。他们证实，那些非人工牙齿是人类的，其中一颗被证明是磨牙。一些较小的骨头被怀疑是人类的手指或脚趾骨，尽管病理学家不能确凿地排除它们来自动物毛孔的可能性。几块头骨碎片被拼合在一起，并确定它们极有可能来自一名高加索男性。这些头骨碎片以及牙齿，是火灾中确实含有残骸的唯一决定性证据。1932年1月7日，斯诺维·罗尔斯（又名约翰·托马斯·史密斯）被正式指控谋杀路易斯·卡隆，并下令进行强制性的验尸官研讯。1月9日，媒体报道称，在前一年的早些时候，斯诺维在马卡萨拉拘留所里曾两次尝试自杀。佩恩警员告诉《西澳大利亚人报》，他发现斯诺维试图在牢房里上吊自杀，此时斯诺维也承认他曾试图服用番木鳖碱，这是一种通常用作杀虫剂的高毒性毒药。

