01:16:07.000 --> 01:17:36.000
On March 30, Snowy's defense counsel, Fred Caron, lodged an appeal against the conviction. He cited that evidence relating to James Ryan and George Lloyd shouldn't have been admitted, and nor should the evidence provided by Arthur Upfield that Snowy was present during a discussion about the disposal method of a fictional victim. Caron also argued there was no evidence that Louis was dead, and claimed that Justice Draper had misdirected the jury, resulting in a miscarriage of justice. The appeal was heard before the Court of Criminal Appeal on April 15, 1932. Two weeks later, it was unanimously dismissed, with the appellate judges disagreeing with Caron's arguments, and pointing out it was Snowy's own legal counsel who initially raised the association with the James Ryan and George Lloyd during the trial. Snowy's legal team then appealed to the High Court of Australia, but this too was rejected, leaving Snowy with no more formal avenues for appeal. A non-denominational Christian organization known as the Groper Brotherhood protested against Snowy's sentence due to their moral objection to the death penalty.
3月30日，斯诺维的辩护律师弗雷德·卡隆对定罪提起了上诉。他指出，有关詹姆斯·赖安和乔治·劳埃德的证据本不应该被采纳，亚瑟·厄普菲尔德提供的关于斯诺维在场参与讨论虚构受害者处理方法的证据也不应该被采纳。卡隆还辩称，没有证据表明路易斯已经死亡，并声称德雷珀法官对陪审团进行了错误指导，导致了司法不公。上诉于1932年4月15日在刑事上诉法院开庭审理。两周后，上诉被一致驳回，上诉法官不同意卡隆的论点，并指出正是斯诺维自己的法律顾问在审判期间最初挑起了与詹姆斯·赖安和乔治·劳埃德的联系。斯诺维的法律团队随后向澳大利亚高等法院提起上诉，但这也遭到拒绝，这使得斯诺维再也没有更多的正式上诉途径。一个名为“格罗珀兄弟会”的无宗派基督教组织因对死刑的道德反对而抗议斯诺维的判决。

60
01:17:36.000 --> 01:18:55.000
A groper is a slang term for people from Western Australia, taken from the name of an insect native to the state. The Groper Brotherhood made a submission to Western Australia's Executive Council, arguing that the death penalty was designed to be reserved for cases of, quote, repulsive willful murder where there are not mitigating circumstances and where no atonement or reformation can be looked for. As the circumstances of Louis Caron's death had never been established and the evidence used to convict Snowy was mostly circumstantial, the Brotherhood argued it wasn't justified to take Snowy's life. They also claimed that a systematic search hadn't been carried out for James Ryan and George Lloyd and therefore the two men shouldn't have been mentioned at Snowy's trial. According to the Brotherhood, he should be granted mercy pending further police activity on their whereabouts. On June 3, 1932, the Attorney General received the Brotherhood's submission, but declined their request. As explained by Terry Walker in his book Murder on the Rabbit-Proof Fence,
“Groper”是西澳大利亚人的俚语，源自该州本土的一种昆虫。Groper兄弟会向西澳大利亚执行委员会提交了一份意见书，主张死刑应仅保留给那些“令人反感、蓄意谋杀且没有减轻罪责的情节，无法寻求赎罪或改造”的案件。由于路易斯·卡伦（Louis Caron）的死因从未查明，且用于给斯诺伊定罪的证据大多是间接证据，兄弟会认为剥夺斯诺伊的生命是不正当的。他们还声称，当局并未对詹姆斯·赖安（James Ryan）和乔治·洛伊德（George Lloyd）展开系统性搜寻，因此在斯诺伊的审判中不应提及这两人。兄弟会认为，在警方进一步调查他们下落期间，应当对斯诺伊予以宽大处理。1932年6月3日，总检察长收到了兄弟会的意见书，但拒绝了他们的请求。正如特里·沃克（Terry Walker）在他的书《防兔栅栏谋杀案》中所解释的那样，

61
01:18:55.000 --> 01:20:15.000
forbidding the use of circumstantial evidence in murder trials would essentially prevent the prosecution of virtually all murders, other than those committed in front of an impartial and reliable witness. Undeterred, the Brotherhood joined forces with the Housewives Association, who viewed themselves as acting on behalf of Snowy's mother. Together, they amended their objection to the circumstantial evidence. They drew up a formal petition, requesting that Mercy be extended to Snowy so that, quote, He may live to atone in the body for the deeds done in the body, and we, as a Christian society, may discharge our creative and reformative responsibilities to the Father of all. The petition was printed and distributed throughout Perth in the hopes of accumulating signatures. On June 4, 1932, Snowy's lawyer Fred Curran held a press conference in which he announced that Snowy had confessed to what really happened to Louis Curran. Snowy had prepared a statement that read,
在谋杀案审判中禁止使用间接证据，基本上会阻止对几乎所有谋杀案的起诉，除非这些谋杀案是在一个公正可靠的目击者面前发生的。兄弟会并未气馁，他们与家庭主妇协会联合起来，后者认为自己是在代表斯诺伊的母亲行事。他们一起修改了对间接证据的异议。他们起草了一份正式请愿书，请求对斯诺伊宽大处理，以便“他能活着为在肉身中犯下的罪行赎罪，而我们作为一个基督教社会，也能对万物之父履行我们的创造和改造责任。”请愿书被印制并分发到整个珀斯，希望能收集到签名。1932年6月4日，斯诺伊的律师弗雷德·卡兰（Fred Curran）举行了一场新闻发布会，宣布斯诺伊已经承认了对路易斯·卡伦真正发生的事情。斯诺伊准备了一份声明，上面写着：

62
01:20:15.000 --> 01:21:39.000
Curran and I were together. It is true that we camped at the old Windemurrah homestead. The police said we didn't camp there, but we did. We were getting short of stores, and Curran asked me to slip into Painesville and cash his check. He didn't sign it. We hadn't any pens and ink. Curran said to me, You can sign it. And I did. When I got back, I found Curran dead. He had apparently eaten by mistake one of our poisoned butterpats, which we had for poisoning foxes. The body was in terrible condition. The crows had been at it. I was in a rotten position. I had just come back from cashing Curran's check. I had a record and was an escaped prisoner. My first impulse was to go and tell the police, but I knew they would take me and put me in prison. So I decided to do away with the body and say nothing about it. The alleged confession seemed to sway many Perth residents, and the petition against Snowy's execution gained 50,000 signatures. However, it was a different story in the outback, where people became even more convinced of Snowy's guilt.
卡兰和我当时在一起。我们的确在旧温德默拉（Windemurrah）宅基地露营过。警察说我们没有在那里露营，但我们的确去了。我们的物资快用完了，卡兰让我溜进佩恩斯维尔（Painesville）去兑现他的支票。他没有在上面签名。我们没有钢笔和墨水。卡兰对我说，你可以代签。于是我照办了。当我回去时，我发现卡兰已经死了。他显然误食了我们用来毒杀狐狸的有毒黄油块之一。尸体状况非常糟糕。乌鸦已经啄食过它了。我的处境糟透了。我刚从兑现卡兰支票的地方回来。我有犯罪前科，而且是个逃犯。我的第一冲动是去告诉警察，但我知道他们会抓我并把我关进监狱。所以我决定处理掉尸体，并且对此外字不提。所谓的自供似乎左右了许多珀斯的居民，反对处决斯诺伊的请愿书获得了5万个签名。然而，内陆的情况却截然不同，那里的人们更加坚信斯诺伊有罪。

