01:21:39.000 --> 01:23:54.000
To them, this version of events seemed utterly impossible, especially considering the Windamara homestead where Snowy claimed Louis had died was 80 kilometers from the camp where his remains were then burned. The petition was submitted to the Attorney General on June 7, 1932, with the Executive Council declining to reprieve Snowy, citing that the law must take its course. The following day, a letter from the Groper Brotherhood appeared in the Daily News announcing the organization felt it had discharged its spiritual obligation and was relieved of any further responsibility. Snowy's execution was scheduled for June 13, 1932. Five days prior, his mother and sister visited him at Fremantle Prison, where they described him as being wasted away to a shadow with sunken eyes. Snowy told his mother that he would rather the death sentence over a life in prison. He was also surprised to learn that his confession to his lawyer had been published, as he had only intended for it to be made public after his death. On June 9, the family of George Lloyd sent a telegram from Adelaide, making a final plea for Snowy to tell the truth about what happened to their loved one, but he declined to offer any information. On June 11, Snowy's lawyer Fred Curran published a letter his client had written to him that served as a final public statement. The letter read, There was no receipt. Things are different up in the north to what they are in town. You take a man's word for it.
对他们来说，这种版本的事件经过显得完全不可能，特别是考虑到斯诺伊声称路易斯去世的温达马拉（Windamara）宅基地，距离后来焚烧其遗骸的营地有80公里远。1932年6月7日，请愿书被提交给总检察长，但执行委员会拒绝暂缓执行斯诺伊的死刑，并称法律必须走其正常的程序。第二天，《每日新闻》上刊登了一封来自Groper兄弟会的信，宣布该组织认为自己已经尽到了精神上的义务，并解除了任何进一步的责任。斯诺伊的死刑定于1932年6月13日执行。就在八天前，他的母亲和妹妹在弗里曼特尔监狱探视了他，据她们描述，他当时已经骨瘦如柴，眼窝深陷。斯诺伊告诉母亲，他宁愿被判死刑，也不愿在监狱里度过余生。当他得知自己向律师作出的供词被公开发表时，他也感到很惊讶，因为他原本只打算在自己死后才将其公之于众。6月9日，乔治·洛伊德的家属从阿德莱德发来电报，最后一次恳求斯诺伊说出关于他们亲人遭遇的真相，但他拒绝提供任何信息。6月11日，斯诺伊的律师弗雷德·卡兰发表了他当事人写给他的一封信，作为最后的公开声明。信中写道：根本没有收据。北方的事情和城里不一样。你得信赖一个人说的话。

64
01:23:54.000 --> 01:26:06.000
What I told you the other day was the truth about Louis Curran. I have never taken a man's life. It is not me who has committed murder, but the law. Death can be no worse than what I have gone through for the last few months. I should have told the truth in the first place, but I had to make a fool of myself and I have to pay for it. The law will be satisfied. I can die with a clear mind. At 8am on June 13, Snowy Rolls was hanged at Fremantle Prison. Some news outlets reported that Rolls made no final statement, yet others asserted that his final words were, I did not kill Louis Curran. Snowy's mother inherited her son's small estate, which included the Dodge truck. She attempted to sell it to a motor wrecker, but the police refused to release the vehicle into her possession, arguing that it technically still belonged to the estate of James Ryan. Given that James never married or had children, he had no known heirs, and the Dodge was eventually auctioned off by the government. The proceeds were placed in a trust in case any of James' heirs ever came forward to claim the money, but none ever did. As a result of the case and its links to Arthur Upfield's novel, interest in Arthur's books surged. During Snowy's trial, his first three books were serialised in Western Australian newspapers, further adding to their popularity. Consequently, Arthur moved to Perth's eastern suburbs and started writing full time. In late 1932, he relocated to a small town in Victoria and began writing articles for the Herald newspaper, before once again travelling the countryside.
我前几天对你说的关于路易斯·卡伦的事都是真的。我从来没有剥夺过任何人的生命。犯下谋杀罪的不是我，而是法律。死亡不会比我过去几个月经历的更糟糕。我本该一开始就说实话，但我却把自己弄得像个傻瓜，我必须为此付出代价。法律会得到满足的。我可以带着清醒的头脑死去。6月13日上午8点，斯诺伊·罗尔斯在弗里曼特尔监狱被绞死。一些新闻媒体报道称罗尔斯没有发表最后声明，但另一些媒体则坚称他的遗言是：“我没有杀死路易斯·卡伦。”斯诺伊的母亲继承了她儿子的微小遗产，其中包括那辆道奇卡车。她试图将其卖给汽车拆解商，但警方拒绝将车辆交到她手上，理由是它从技术上讲仍然属于詹姆斯·赖安的遗产。鉴于詹姆斯从未结婚或生育子女，他没有已知的继承人，这辆道奇最终被政府拍卖。所得款项被存入一个信托基金中，以防詹姆士的任何继承人日后现身索取这笔钱，但从来没有人来过。由于该案及其与亚瑟·阿普菲尔德（Arthur Upfield）小说的联系，人们对亚瑟的书籍的兴趣激增。在斯诺伊受审期间，他的前三本书在西澳大利亚的报纸上连载，进一步提高了它们的人气。因此，亚瑟搬到了珀斯的东郊，开始全职写作。1932年末，他搬到了维多利亚州的一个小镇，开始为《先驱报》撰写文章，之后再次开始在乡间游历。

